  "name": "loss_logsigmoid_e1_cost_balanced_m3",
  "intuition": "The failure indicates the environment's expects schema requires keys named 'log_prob_w' and 'log_prob_l'. To stabilize and simplify, keep the core numerically stable pairwise objective `-logsigmoid(x)` with explicit clamping of logits, and make cost adjustment strictly optional and detached. Also add a safe fallback to infer winner/loser log-probs from common alternative key names if present, preventing missing-key errors while preserving preference semantics.",
  "pseudocode": "lpw, lpl = required log-probs (with simple alias fallback)
x = alpha*scale*(lpw-lpl)
if cost keys exist: x -= cost_coef*clamp(detach(cost_b-cost_a), -gap_clip, gap_clip)
